  "comments": [
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5500d7a_fddbfbb5",
        "filename": "android/packaging.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 423,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-27T19:14:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We would like to remove the rules that copy files to the \"full install path\", because if there are multiple modules that get installed to the same location, those rules conflict, even if they\u0027re never included on the same device.\n\nInstead of adding them as implicit deps here, could you make the filesystem module do the copy as it\u0027s being built? This could be done by adding the \"full install\" directories to `dirsToSpecs` during `copyPackagingSpecs`, but don\u0027t you also need to copy the other, non-packagingspec files too?",
      "revId": "ce7fa01e0d6f5bb8ff3345ba57ba51fcb4cdc062",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1eec3a69_eba1be4f",
        "filename": "android/packaging.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 423,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146974
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-28T01:17:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But this `cmd.Implicit(ps.fullInstallPath)` does not make additional rule to generate the file in `fullInstallPath` but to trigger the existing rule. I added this dependency to avoid the rule conflict to generate the `fullInstallPath` files.\n\n\u003e Instead of adding them as implicit deps here, could you make the filesystem module do the copy as it\u0027s being built?\n\nI think your suggestion to install the filesystem files to `fullInstallPath` during `copyPackagingSpecs` generates new rules to install files to `fullInstallPath`. The new rules will cause the rule conflict with the original install rules, won\u0027t they?\nThe `droid` target requires the files in `fullInstallPath` and we already have the rules for them.\n\n\u003e but don\u0027t you also need to copy the other, non-packagingspec files too?\n\nYes, and they are the more difficult part to address. (.fsv_meta, aconfig files..) Each must be resolved differently by ignoring make rules and using soong rules to install them to the `fullInstallPath`. This is also to avoid the rule conflict.",
      "parentUuid": "f5500d7a_fddbfbb5",
      "revId": "ce7fa01e0d6f5bb8ff3345ba57ba51fcb4cdc062",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b38201e_57d64732",
        "filename": "android/packaging.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 423,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-28T18:01:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am suggesting to do the copy without a rule for it. `copyPackagingSpecs` / `CopySpecsToDirs` doesn\u0027t actually make rules that output the copied files, it just does the copying. That way you won\u0027t get conflicts. It will also prevent other rules from depending on these files, but that\u0027s desirable. The main reason we have the rules normally is so that make can depend on them and build the images from them, but with soong-built images it\u0027s not needed.\n\nYou could also do the copy on the whole staging directory after `buildAconfigFlagsFiles` so that the non-packagingspec files are also copied.",
      "parentUuid": "1eec3a69_eba1be4f",
      "revId": "ce7fa01e0d6f5bb8ff3345ba57ba51fcb4cdc062",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01399236_b4a540ed",
        "filename": "android/packaging.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 423,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146974
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-29T06:47:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I got your point. But that will break the user journey of `m \u003cmodule-name\u003e \u0026\u0026 adb sync`. To allow the scenario, I think we still need to maintain the rule for the `fullInstallPath` in `$(PRODUCT_OUT)`.",
      "parentUuid": "1b38201e_57d64732",
      "revId": "ce7fa01e0d6f5bb8ff3345ba57ba51fcb4cdc062",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1887d9ea_b7228b1e",
        "filename": "android/packaging.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 423,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-29T17:53:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, breaking `m \u003cmodule-name\u003e \u0026\u0026 adb sync` is intentional. It used to be that `m \u003cmodule-name\u003e \u0026\u0026 m \u0026\u0026 fastboot flashall` would install the module as well, but I\u0027ve already fixed that.\n\nThe fact that `m \u003cmodule-name\u003e` installs module to the staging directory is an unfortunate side effect. It makes it confusing for users who are now installing extra stuff onto the device that wouldn\u0027t be installed if you did a clean build.",
      "parentUuid": "01399236_b4a540ed",
      "revId": "ce7fa01e0d6f5bb8ff3345ba57ba51fcb4cdc062",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b83798a7_4fc0f821",
        "filename": "android/packaging.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 423,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146974
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-29T23:25:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I still think users expect that `m \u003cmodule-name\u003e` will build and update the files in `$(PRODUCT_OUT)` (even for the already installed files).\nWhat will be the target rule for `m \u003cmodule-name\u003e` with the soong filesystem? Or do you think we can remove supporting `m \u003cmodule-name\u003e` with the soong filesystem?",
      "parentUuid": "1887d9ea_b7228b1e",
      "revId": "ce7fa01e0d6f5bb8ff3345ba57ba51fcb4cdc062",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b5c3379_266bab38",
        "filename": "android/packaging.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 423,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-29T23:31:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`m \u003cmodule-name\u003e` would just build the `out/soong/.intermediates` files for that module. And for host tools it would still add them to the PATH. For apps, you could still `adb install` them but using the `out/soong/.intermediates` path instead. For more core system modules, building them individually would essentially just be a check that it compiles, there\u0027s not much you can do with them without building the whole device.",
      "parentUuid": "b83798a7_4fc0f821",
      "revId": "ce7fa01e0d6f5bb8ff3345ba57ba51fcb4cdc062",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "65bc0e1f_357f8565",
        "filename": "android/packaging.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 423,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-30T08:36:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Cole,\n\nI agree with you on that `m \u003cmodule\u003e` being installed to `PRODUCT_OUT` was a bad design. But, what\u0027s happened is what\u0027s happened and we can\u0027t ignore the fact that existing developer workflow depend on this. We can\u0027t break them all at a sudden.\n\nA typical workflow is as follows.\n\n1. `\u003cmodule\u003e` is already in `PRODUCT_PACKAGES`. (ex: libc, libm, libdl)\n2. initially, `m \u0026\u0026 fastboot flashall`.\n3. make some changes, then, `m \u003cmodule\u003e`\n4. then, `adb sync` or `adevice`\n\nYes, people could have done `m` instead of `m \u003cmodule\u003e` at step 3. But it can be very long if `\u003cmodule\u003e` is close to the root of the dependency tree. You don\u0027t want to spend time on rebuilding every apks when you add a logging statement somewhere in `framework/base/core`.",
      "parentUuid": "9b5c3379_266bab38",
      "revId": "ce7fa01e0d6f5bb8ff3345ba57ba51fcb4cdc062",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c4559683_0df6007c",
        "filename": "android/packaging.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 423,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146974
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-30T13:00:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With the `adb sync` test, I noticed that the files in `$PRODUCT_OUT` does not have the same timestamp with those in the soong-built system image. We cannot match the timestamps with the \"Implicit\" dependency.\n\nTo enable the `adb sync`:\n1. copy with preserve option from `soong/.intermediate` to `$PRODUCT_OUT` (Cole\u0027s suggestion)\n2. create image from `$PRODUCT_OUT` instead of `soong/.intermediate`.\n3. use `adevice`\n\nOption 1 is the simplest solution (aosp/3247732) but has the concern for `m \u003cmodule\u003e`,\nOption 2 requires major modification on copy and packaging functions.\n\nHowever, I also agree with keeping the `m \u003cmodule\u003e` feature that I myself is using. Also I noticed that the fuzz test is using `m \u003cfuzz_test\u003e \u0026\u0026 adb sync data` commands. (https://source.android.com/docs/security/test/libfuzzer#write-a-fuzzer)\n\nSo, I think Option 1 cannot be the final solution.",
      "parentUuid": "65bc0e1f_357f8565",
      "revId": "ce7fa01e0d6f5bb8ff3345ba57ba51fcb4cdc062",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ad71540e_2ed1c078",
        "filename": "android/packaging.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 423,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-30T17:52:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not suggesting we break `m \u003cmodule\u003e` -\u003e `$PRODUCT_OUT` right now. I\u0027m just requesting that we don\u0027t make the soong-built partitions rely on this functionality.\n\nI have two ideas for how to support `m \u003cmodule\u003e` -\u003e `$PRODUCT_OUT` in the long term:\n - Make the copying happen outside of the build, like by soong_ui\n - Do something similar to how `dist` works: make a `stage` target, so you could do `m \u003cmodule\u003e stage`. The staging would be done in a smaller ninja file that would be regenerated whenever the list of modules to stage on the command line changes.",
      "parentUuid": "c4559683_0df6007c",
      "revId": "ce7fa01e0d6f5bb8ff3345ba57ba51fcb4cdc062",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e944d60_79c22d77",
        "filename": "android/packaging.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 423,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-02T09:40:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e requesting that we don\u0027t make the soong-built partitions rely on this functionality.\n\nYes, that\u0027s a very fair reason. Then how about this?\n\nThis filesystem module produces the list of module name it would install in it. Then Make uses that to install those modules to PRODUCT_OUT?",
      "parentUuid": "ad71540e_2ed1c078",
      "revId": "ce7fa01e0d6f5bb8ff3345ba57ba51fcb4cdc062",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a89867d4_d043aeb2",
        "filename": "android/packaging.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 423,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146974
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-03T01:47:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I\u0027m just requesting that we don\u0027t make the soong-built partitions rely on this functionality.\n\nThen the option 1 that I implemented with aosp/3247732 works for this purpose. `m \u003cmodule\u003e` still works with the change.\n\nWe may design a long-term solution when building all partitions from soong.",
      "parentUuid": "7e944d60_79c22d77",
      "revId": "ce7fa01e0d6f5bb8ff3345ba57ba51fcb4cdc062",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
